Feature docs for the `game` product (game-client + game-server), the `docs/{service}/{feature}.md` convention in docs/claude/work-item-workflow.md; moved here from docs/features/ on 2026-10-31, so older plans and the mobile repo may still say the old path. Most files are developer notes; library-sync.md, organizations.md and scripting-and-sharing.md are user guides written before end-user docs got their own home in each service's help area. plugin-config.md (2026-10-31) is the developer note on how plugin settings are stored: overrides only, one pruning write funnel in usePlugins.ts, a one-time prune of old frozen saves. The contribute.md file outlines how players can submit data to the Shattered Archive project, while questbot.md describes automation features for quest cycles. The user-equipment.md and user-library.md files document character equipment tracking and a React component structure respectively, all serving as reference materials for developers and contributors working on the project's core systems. library-sync.md (2026-08) is the player-facing companion to user-library.md, covering Library-content cloud sync (parchment/notes/books) across web, mobile, and the site's "My Writings" page, including how per-account encryption at rest works in plain terms. organizations.md (2026-08) documents the Organizations feature, now fully COMPLETE (Phase 2, all 7 steps, live-verified end to end across web/game-client/mobile) — kingdoms/clans/religions/friend groups, playing as a character with one-org-per-category (auto-leave on a same-category move), account-level admin roles for cross-org access, invites vs. join requests, leave/remove vs. account-wide bans, shared org content in nested folders, an audit log, append-only revision history with web-only revert, per-group envelope-key encryption with rotation on any access loss. Org management (create/invite/roles/bans) and revision history/audit stay website-only by design; browsing + role-gated content editing works on all three clients (Library → Organizations on web, a Library tab on game-client, a More-menu screen on mobile).
autopilot.md (2026-11-13): the autopilot wizard data layer, record kinds, target overrides and sync contract.
